# Illustration template

Every generated image for this project uses the vintage editorial ink style. Fill the
brackets and send this as the prompt, unchanged otherwise:

```
A [OBJECT] drawn as a vintage editorial ink illustration: bold black hand-inked
outlines with slightly varied line weight, fine crosshatch shading, realistic
material detail ([MATERIAL 1, e.g. walnut wood grain], [MATERIAL 2, e.g. brushed
steel with specular highlights], aged cream paper with stacked sheets and a
curled corner). Slight 3/4 tilt, about 8 degrees. Muted palette of cream, warm
brown, steel gray and black, with a single forest green (#2f5d46) accent on
[ACCENT DETAIL]. Minimal readable text: only the word "[LABEL]". Isolated on a
pure white background, no cast shadow, no scenery, centered, icon composition.
```

## Brackets

- `[OBJECT]` — the subject, named plainly ("a clipboard holding a draft list").
- `[MATERIAL 1]` / `[MATERIAL 2]` — the two materials to render with real texture.
- `[ACCENT DETAIL]` — the one element that gets the forest green; everything else
  stays in the muted palette.
- `[LABEL]` — one word of readable text, or drop the text sentence entirely.

## Using the result

The art comes back on white, so it needs a light plate to sit on in this dark UI.
Hand-drawn SVG is still fine for line-art UI icons such as nav glyphs; this template
covers illustrations and image assets.
